# Project Intelligence: minimaxh3

- Read all files in memory-bank/ at session start; techContext.md has the machine-specific gotchas.
- GPU is shared: `vllm.service` (user systemd) normally occupies ~93GB VRAM. Stop it before
  generation, and remember the user's Qwen endpoint on port 8000 goes down when you do.
- Always use `HF_HOME=~/.cache/hf` — the default HF cache is root-owned and sudo is interactive.
- diffusers is pinned to a PR commit; MiniMax-H3 is not in a diffusers release yet.
- FL2VA vs Ref2VA: different transformer partitions (`transformer/` vs `transformer_ref/`).
  Build with `build_pipeline(..., task="ref2va")` / `--ref KIND:PATH`. Do not keep both
  resident — host RAM cannot hold two 62GB transformers plus the conditioner.
- Ref2VA limits are 9 graphic/image refs, 3 video refs, 3 audio refs, and 12
  total. Preserve upload order because prompts address them as `<Picture 1>`, etc.
- REST image references use `reference_image_urls`; never echo signed URLs in
  status. Reference mode is mutually exclusive with FL2VA keyframes. Turbo on
  Ref2VA is experimental: the module layout accepts the FL2VA-trained LoRA, but
  always warn that identity fidelity may be reduced.
- Turbo is the default for UI, REST, CLI, and Brightify H3 jobs. Preserve an
  explicit full-quality opt-out (`turbo=false` / `--no-turbo`).
- Brightify production requests may specify output width/height/duration.
  Normalize after generation, on CPU in bounded resize chunks, before encoding.
- REST priority is lower-first and non-preemptive: production defaults to 100,
  local CLI tests use 0, and sequence order preserves FIFO ties.
- Before each denoiser forward, offload every other ComponentsManager module.
  A resident pipe otherwise leaves the ~32GB conditioner on CUDA; Ref2VA then
  OOMs around 93GB. Four-ref ~10s turbo jobs should generate at 416×736 (or
  similar) and normalize up, not 544×960.
- Keep the server pipeline resident for later jobs of the same task. Do not
  discard after every REST job: that drops the Python handle without returning
  ~89GB of VRAM, then the next load fails its own free-VRAM check. Count only
  foreign processes in that check. Mode switches still detach hooks without
  calling `offload()`; full CPU offload reaches 121GB RSS and triggers the
  host OOM killer.
- User prefers single quotes for static CLI arguments.
